WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.859
- You know, it's so funny, I
get this question all the time.

00:00:03.859 --> 00:00:06.467
Do you still remember
how it felt to drown?

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:10.634
It was a crippling feeling, I
was suffocating underwater.

00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:14.819
Now I've made it my job to conquer my fear

00:00:14.819 --> 00:00:16.949
and to help to get these kids swim lessons

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.139
and to learn how to respect the water.

00:00:19.139 --> 00:00:21.806
(calming music)

00:00:27.158 --> 00:00:29.846
My name is Cullen Jones, I
was in the Olympics in 2008

00:00:29.846 --> 00:00:32.469
and 2012 and I love to give swim lessons.

00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:33.899
- [Announcer] Cullen Jones is a four-time

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:36.768
Olympic medalist swimmer for team USA.

00:00:36.768 --> 00:00:38.949
- [Cullen] Right after getting
the gold medal in 2008,

00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:41.168
they put the drowning rates in front of me

00:00:41.168 --> 00:00:43.488
and I learned that 70%
of African Americans,

00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:47.462
nearly 60% of Latin Americans
and nearly 40% of Caucasians

00:00:47.462 --> 00:00:48.662
don't know how to swim.

00:00:48.662 --> 00:00:51.009
So it's a big problem all over the US.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:52.919
I think the reason that
we don't see as many

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.078
African Americans in swimming is because

00:00:55.078 --> 00:00:58.638
there's such a stigma that
black people don't swim

00:00:58.638 --> 00:01:00.229
and this is something that needs to be broken

00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:02.868
because we are losing
children, we are losing adults,

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:07.029
and it's something that can
be changed by swim lessons.

00:01:07.029 --> 00:01:08.871
So when I want you guys to kick,

00:01:08.871 --> 00:01:13.289
I want you guys to push your
arms right above the water.

00:01:13.289 --> 00:01:16.660
Swimming lessons are so important
to kids to me personally

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.660
because I was almost one of those kids

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.991
and part of the statistic.

00:01:20.991 --> 00:01:22.820
- [Announcer] When Cullen
was just five years old,

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.791
he almost drowned on a water
slide at an amusement park.

00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:28.340
- They had to come out and
grab me and resuscitate me

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.231
because I was underwater
for about 30 seconds.

00:01:30.231 --> 00:01:32.489
I think what's important
about this story is that

00:01:32.489 --> 00:01:35.180
I was fully supervised,
I mean, it was that easy

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.098
and that quick for me to go underwater.

00:01:37.098 --> 00:01:39.260
That could have been my
last day on this earth.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.159
- [Announcer] And with
that near-death experience

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:42.649
Cullen has made it his platform to bring

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:46.089
water safety education to
kids from all backgrounds.

00:01:46.089 --> 00:01:47.420
- Back stroke.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.869
The way that I'm trying
to change my community

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:51.159
is definitely with working with the

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:52.588
Make a Splash Initiative.

00:01:52.588 --> 00:01:54.177
I knew this was my way
of giving back to a sport

00:01:54.177 --> 00:01:56.279
that has given me so much.

00:01:56.279 --> 00:01:58.297
Once you learn how to swim,
it's like riding a bike,

00:01:58.297 --> 00:01:59.848
you never forget.

00:01:59.848 --> 00:02:03.098
So take the time and learn how to swim.

